# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the FCIDump data into a fermionic operator and applies normal ordering to simplify the operator structure.\n"
msgstr "Menukar data FCIDump kepada operator fermionik dan menggunakan susunan normal untuk memudahkan struktur operator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Group terms by electronic structure {#group-terms-by-electronic-structure}"
msgstr "Kumpulkan sebutan mengikut struktur elektronik {#group-terms-by-electronic-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Groups related Hamiltonian terms by electronic structure before constructing their evolution circuits.\n"
msgstr "Mengumpulkan sebutan Hamiltonian yang berkaitan mengikut struktur elektronik sebelum membina litar evolusi mereka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate sampling weights, then normalize and map to qubit operators {#calculate-sampling-weights-then-normalize-and-map-to-qubit-operators}"
msgstr "Kira pemberat persampelan, kemudian normalkan dan petakan kepada operator qubit {#calculate-sampling-weights-then-normalize-and-map-to-qubit-operators}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Order matters here.** Normalization rescales every coefficient to unit magnitude *in place*, so the sampling weights must be computed first. If normalization runs first, every $|c_j|$ reads back as exactly `1.0` and each group's weight collapses into a bare count of its terms — the sampling distribution would then be driven by group size rather than by the physical coefficients.\n"
msgstr "**Susunan penting di sini.** Normalisasi menskala semula setiap pekali kepada magnitud unit *di tempat*, jadi pemberat persampelan mesti dikira dahulu. Jika normalisasi dijalankan dahulu, setiap $|c_j|$ akan terbaca semula sebagai tepat `1.0` dan pemberat setiap kumpulan runtuh menjadi sekadar kiraan sebutannya — taburan persampelan kemudiannya akan didorong oleh saiz kumpulan dan bukannya oleh pekali fizikal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each group's weight is the **mean** absolute coefficient of its terms. The Python tab's `QDriftTrotterization` pass uses the same weight for a grouped Hamiltonian. Using the sum instead would make $\\lambda$ scale with group size, which in turn skews the evolution time $t_k = \\lambda\\tau/n$.\n"
msgstr "Pemberat setiap kumpulan ialah pekali mutlak **min** bagi sebutannya. Laluan `QDriftTrotterization` pada tab Python menggunakan pemberat yang sama untuk Hamiltonian berkumpulan. Menggunakan hasil tambah sebaliknya akan menyebabkan $\\lambda$ berskala dengan saiz kumpulan, yang seterusnya mencondongkan masa evolusi $t_k = \\lambda\\tau/n$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The weight $\\lambda_i = \\frac{1}{|G_i|}\\sum_{j \\in G_i} |c_{ij}|$ is the mean absolute coefficient over the terms of group $G_i$, read from the original coefficients. Normalization then rescales each fermionic term to unit magnitude before the Jordan-Wigner transformation, preserving only its phase/sign in the evolved operator. This matches qDRIFT's normalized-term evolution: coefficient magnitudes determine sampling probabilities via $\\lambda$, while the circuit evolution uses the normalized term so large coefficients are not counted twice.\n"
msgstr "Pemberat $\\lambda_i = \\frac{1}{|G_i|}\\sum_{j \\in G_i} |c_{ij}|$ ialah pekali mutlak min bagi sebutan kumpulan $G_i$, dibaca daripada pekali asal. Normalisasi kemudian menskala semula setiap sebutan fermionik kepada magnitud unit sebelum transformasi Jordan-Wigner, dengan hanya mengekalkan fasa/tandanya dalam operator yang dievolusikan. Ini sepadan dengan evolusi sebutan ternormal qDRIFT: magnitud pekali menentukan kebarangkalian persampelan melalui $\\lambda$, manakala evolusi litar menggunakan sebutan ternormal supaya pekali besar tidak dikira dua kali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample operator sets {#sample-operator-sets}"
msgstr "Sampel set operator {#sample-operator-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Draws the operator sets for 100 random circuits, each containing 10 groups sampled from the weighted distribution. The next step turns these sets into the ensemble of qDRIFT circuits.\n"
msgstr "Melukis set operator untuk 100 litar rawak, setiap satu mengandungi 10 kumpulan yang disampel daripada taburan berpemberat. Langkah seterusnya menukar set ini menjadi ensembel litar qDRIFT.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Build the qDRIFT circuits (C++) {#step-2-build-the-qdrift-circuits-c}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Bina litar qDRIFT (C++) {#step-2-build-the-qdrift-circuits-c}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the C++ version, this step builds the circuits from the sampled operator sets. Transpilation for the target backend happens in Step 3, immediately before each circuit is submitted.\n"
msgstr "Dalam versi C++, langkah ini membina litar daripada set operator yang disampel. Transpilasi untuk backend sasaran berlaku dalam Langkah 3, sejurus sebelum setiap litar dihantar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The complete program then prints circuit statistics and the operator indices of circuit 0, which are omitted here.\n"
msgstr "Program lengkap kemudian mencetak statistik litar dan indeks operator bagi litar 0, yang ditinggalkan di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each sampled operator, creates a Suzuki-Trotter evolution circuit with time $t_k = \\frac{\\lambda \\tau}{n}$, where $n$ is the number of operators sampled per circuit and $\\tau$ is the time step. Because each sampled group was normalized term-by-term before mapping, this evolution applies only the phase/sign of each term during the rotation; the magnitudes contribute through the sampling distribution only. The Hartree-Fock initial state is prepared by applying X gates to qubits 0-6 and 10-16 (seven electrons in each spin sector). Each evolution circuit's instructions are manually appended to the main circuit using the C++ API.\n"
msgstr "Bagi setiap operator yang disampel, mencipta litar evolusi Suzuki-Trotter dengan masa $t_k = \\frac{\\lambda \\tau}{n}$, dengan $n$ ialah bilangan operator yang disampel bagi setiap litar dan $\\tau$ ialah langkah masa. Oleh sebab setiap kumpulan yang disampel dinormalkan sebutan demi sebutan sebelum pemetaan, evolusi ini hanya menggunakan fasa/tanda setiap sebutan semasa putaran; magnitud hanya menyumbang melalui taburan persampelan. Keadaan awal Hartree-Fock disediakan dengan menggunakan get X pada qubit 0-6 dan 10-16 (tujuh elektron dalam setiap sektor spin). Arahan setiap litar evolusi ditambah secara manual pada litar utama menggunakan API C++.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives (C++) {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-c}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit (C++) {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives-c}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Connects to IBM Quantum, selects the backend by name, transpiles each circuit for that backend, and submits **one job per circuit**: 100 separate Sampler jobs of 100 shots each on a 20-qubit register. It then polls each job until it finishes and collects the bitstrings from `result[0]`. Every job uses QPU time and waits in the queue separately, so expect this step to take much longer than a single batched job.\n"
msgstr "Menyambung ke IBM Quantum, memilih backend mengikut nama, mentranspil setiap litar untuk backend itu, dan menghantar **satu kerja bagi setiap litar**: 100 kerja Sampler berasingan dengan 100 tembakan setiap satu pada daftar 20 qubit. Kemudian ia membuat pengundian setiap kerja sehingga selesai dan mengumpul rentetan bit daripada `result[0]`. Setiap kerja menggunakan masa QPU dan menunggu dalam baris gilir secara berasingan, jadi jangkakan langkah ini mengambil masa yang jauh lebih lama daripada satu kerja kelompok tunggal.\n"

